Translation patch: `ColumnIndex for &str`

Change: The loop `for (i, c) in columns.iter().enumerate() { if c.name_ref() == self.as_bytes() { return Some(i) } } None` becomes `column_idx_by_name(str_as_bytes(self), columns, 0)`, a new recursive helper: at `i < columns.len()` it returns `Some(i)` if `columns[i].name_ref() == name` and otherwise recurses on `i + 1`; at `i == columns.len()` it returns `None`. `self.as_bytes()` goes through the existing opaque helper `value::convert::trusted::str_as_bytes` (patch 40, modelled exactly in FunsExternal.lean).
Why: Aeneas reports "Found a case of unsupported nested borrows" for the loop (`self` is a `&&str`, and each `Column` holds an `Arc<ColumnMeta<'static>>`, as in patch 30); it models neither `enumerate` (patches 04/05) nor `str::as_bytes`.
Behaviour: Identical: the first index whose column name equals the bytes of `self`, or `None`. Stack: the recursion goes once per column, so the patched copy uses O(columns) stack where the loop uses constant stack (as in patch 30); stack exhaustion is not modelled. This difference exists only in the translated copy.

diff --git a/src/row/mod.rs b/src/row/mod.rs
index 5b69311..fb6ad1c 100644
--- a/src/row/mod.rs
+++ b/src/row/mod.rs
@@ -251,11 +251,24 @@ impl ColumnIndex for usize {
 
 impl ColumnIndex for &'_ str {
     fn idx(&self, columns: &[Column]) -> Option<usize> {
-        for (i, c) in columns.iter().enumerate() {
-            if c.name_ref() == self.as_bytes() {
-                return Some(i);
-            }
+        column_idx_by_name(
+            crate::value::convert::trusted::str_as_bytes(self),
+            columns,
+            0,
+        )
+    }
+}
+
+/// The loop `for (i, c) in columns.iter().enumerate() { .. }` of `ColumnIndex for &str`, written
+/// as a recursion on `i`: the index of the first column among `i..` named `name`.
+fn column_idx_by_name(name: &[u8], columns: &[Column], i: usize) -> Option<usize> {
+    if i < columns.len() {
+        if columns[i].name_ref() == name {
+            Some(i)
+        } else {
+            column_idx_by_name(name, columns, i + 1)
         }
+    } else {
         None
     }
 }
